  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Research on local tiger nut varieties productivity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective is to study and test local varietal ecotypes of tiger nuts with high yields and milk content, stimulating the dissemination of these varieties to ensure a steady supply of tiger nut milk and its derivatives.This study complements the SDGP &quot;Chain Booster&quot; program funded by the Embassy of the Netherlands in Niger and the Netherlands Enterprise Agency (RVO), concerning the improvement of the tiger nut sector and the establishment of a tiger nut milk production plant. The research aims to identify a variety of tiger nuts with a high yield and milk content, and share results with tiger nut producers and processors.The project will be implement in Maradi, the tiger nut niche of production.</narrative>
  </description>
